{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>And he shall come to the south</b> — it is the region of Egypt." "<b>And the sense of \"and it shall not be as the former or as the latter\"</b> — for in the first coming he did all his will, and likewise in the latter coming, which is the third, in which he destroyed the Temple, also Egypt; for in the second coming, which is the middle one, he will be weak. And thus it is written: <b>and they shall come against him</b> — \"and peoples shall come.\""], :book :daniel, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {1 "The phrase 'כי בביאה השניה היא האמצעי,ת' has a suspect point or letter after 'האמצעי'; read as 'האמצעית' (the middle one, fem.). The logic is compressed: in the middle campaign his power was diminished."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Daniel - Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/daniel"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:21:17.979716765Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}